<QuestionLayout
  title='What does "device-independent" mean in Traverse?'
  description="A device-independent capability is a WASM binary that runs unmodified on any client that loads it, executing locally by default and delegating to a server only when the client's own context calls for it."
  canonical="https://traverse-framework.com/questions/what-does-device-independent-mean-in-traverse.html"
